const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"价格怎样逐步吸收私人信息？",en:"How does private information enter prices?"},body:{zh:"Kyle研究一个知情交易者不会一次性暴露全部信息的市场。价格如何在连续交易中逐渐反映信息，取决于知情者的交易选择，以及做市者从订单流中能推断出多少。",en:"Kyle studies a market in which an informed trader need not reveal information all at once. Price discovery depends on the trader's order choices and on what market makers can infer from the resulting order flow."}},{title:{zh:"每次拍卖先提交数量，再确定价格",en:"Quantities precede pricing in each auction"},body:{zh:"模型中知情者与噪声交易者先同时选择数量，做市者随后观察合并后的订单流并定价。做市者看不到两类交易的单独数量，知情者下单时也不知道当次噪声订单。把这些信息集合分清，才能理解噪声为何掩护私人信息，以及价格为何随订单流更新。",en:"The insider and noise traders choose quantities simultaneously; market makers then observe combined order flow and set a price. Makers cannot separate the two components, and the insider does not know the current noise order when choosing a quantity. These information sets explain both concealment and price updating."},reference:{url:"https://people.duke.edu/~qc2/BA532/1985%20EMA%20Kyle.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第1节：两步拍卖与信息集合",en:"Original §1: two-step auction and information sets"}}},{title:{zh:"三个角色构成一个机制",en:"Three roles, one mechanism"},body:{zh:"模型包含单一风险中性的知情者、随机噪声交易者和竞争性的风险中性做市者。噪声交易让知情交易混入普通订单，做市者则根据观察到的交易更新价格。缺少这些角色和假设，就不能把任何成交量变化都叫作模型中的信息交易。",en:"The model contains one risk-neutral insider, random noise traders and competitive risk-neutral market makers. Noise trading conceals informed orders, while market makers update prices from observed flow. These roles and assumptions are not interchangeable with generic changes in trading volume."}},{title:{zh:"均衡结果有条件",en:"Equilibrium results are conditional"},body:{zh:"出版方摘要描述了连续交易极限下的结果：市场深度在模型中保持不变，私人信息到交易结束时进入价格。这些是特定模型下推导的性质，不是对现实每一个交易日的描述。",en:"The publisher's abstract describes constant market depth and incorporation of private information by the end of trading in the continuous-trading limit. These are properties derived under the model, not descriptions of every real trading session."}},{title:{zh:"这里的深度不是盘口档位数量",en:"Model depth is not a count of order-book levels"},body:{zh:"做市者按其信息条件下的资产清算价值期望定价，订单流因此与价格变化联系起来。连续交易极限中的恒定深度是这一均衡的性质，不是承诺现实盘口总有同样厚度。编辑建议：实证代理应写清交易方向、价格变化和采样间隔，不能用总成交量直接替代模型订单流。",en:"Competitive makers price at expected liquidation value conditional on their information, linking flow to price changes. Constant depth in the continuous limit is an equilibrium property, not a claim that displayed books always have equal thickness. Editorial application: specify trade direction, price changes and sampling; aggregate volume is not the model's signed flow."},reference:{url:"https://people.duke.edu/~qc2/BA532/1985%20EMA%20Kyle.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第1节：竞争性定价与连续交易极限",en:"Original §1: competitive pricing and continuous limit"}}},{title:{zh:"从模型走到数据，还缺什么？",en:"What is missing when moving to data?"},body:{zh:"本站建议用它理解价格冲击与信息披露速度之间的联系，再单独核对实际数据能观察什么。分钟价格与总成交量并不直接提供交易方向、交易者身份或盘口深度；仅凭它们不能验证模型中的每一个机制。",en:"Use the model to organize questions about price impact and the speed of information revelation, then audit observability separately. Minute prices and aggregate volume do not directly reveal trade direction, trader identity or order-book depth, and cannot test every mechanism on their own."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"这是理论模型导读，不是内幕交易识别方法。单一知情者、风险中性等假设限制了向复杂现实市场的直接迁移。",en:"This is a guide to a theoretical model, not an insider-trading detector. Assumptions such as one informed trader and risk neutrality limit direct transfer to complex markets."}};export{e as default};
